# ── EVIDENCE IS A RECORD, NOT SOURCE ──────────────────────────────────────
#
# `docs/work-done/**-EVIDENCE/` holds what was measured at the time: captured
# HTML, probe output, and `.json` files whose first line is a `### header`
# naming the URL and cache mode the numbers below it came from. Prettier cannot
# parse those and `pnpm lint` — which is `prettier --check .` — has therefore
# been RED on master since 27 Aug 2026, on 7 committed files, for reasons no
# incoming change caused and no incoming change can fix.
#
# A permanently-red gate is worse than no gate: it trains everyone to run
# `lint:fix` instead, and `lint:fix` is `prettier --write .` — which on
# 28 Ogos 2026 silently rewrote 117 files across three prior sprints'
# evidence directories while a single route file was being formatted. Rewriting
# the record of what was measured is not a formatting change; it is editing
# the evidence after the fact.
#
# So the record is ignored, and the gate is green for the reason it should be.
docs/work-done

# ── A FIXTURE IS INPUT TO A MEASUREMENT, NOT SOURCE ───────────────────────
#
# `tests/ui-layout-gate/fixtures/` holds production HTML captured while it was
# broken, the CSS and fonts that make its 44px column exist at all, and a
# hand-built page whose cases the self-test asserts exact counts against.
# Reformatting any of it changes what the gate measures — the same reason
# `docs/work-done` is ignored above, one step earlier in the pipeline.
tests/ui-layout-gate/fixtures
